e and Ezek 9. In 9:6, zaqen is used to refer to both elders and old man. The absence of the article opens the way for the same to be true here."],[5,11,"Variant because kurios is anarthrous in LXX. Topical, so theos should have article!"],[5,14,"In Hebrew, the verb is clearly focal. If 'lording it over' (v 3) presupposes being proud, then the verb is the DFE here, too."],[6,5,"Articular relates to suffering - see Dubis."],[6,9,"'You', rather than God, are the topic: distinct point. 'God' is default propositional topic, which is cancelled (?) by P1 constituent."],[8,3,"Adjectival usage - several grammarians treat it as such. This explains the absence of the article with diabolos (variant exists)."],[8,11,"Taken as an embedded question, so default order."],[9,7,"the same experiences of the devil as a roaring lion; viz., of the sufferings."],[9,12,"Particularly if anarthrous."],[10,4,"anarthrous: multi-faceted, could be looking forward, rather than backward."],[12,2,"The appositive constituent could be a continuation of the initial P2 constituent. Within the apposition, is topical."]],"o":[[5,11,5,14],[5,15,5,18]]}}